.TH XScreenSaver 1 "09-Jun-2026" "X Version 11"
.SH NAME
mystify \- animate bouncing, deforming wire polygons
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mystify
[\-\-display \fIhost:display.screen\fP]
[\-\-window]
[\-\-root]
[\-\-window\-id \fInumber\fP]
[\-\-delay \fImicroseconds\fP]
[\-\-polys \fInumber\fP]
[\-\-points \fInumber\fP]
[\-\-trails \fInumber\fP]
[\-\-speed \fInumber\fP]
[\-\-thickness \fIpixels\fP]
[\-\-colors \fInumber\fP]
[\-\-seed \fInumber\fP]
[\-\-fps]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.I mystify
program animates deforming wire polygons whose corners move independently and
change speed when they bounce from the edges of the window.
.PP
It is inspired by the Windows 95 and Windows 98
``Mystify Your Mind'' screen saver.
.PP
Instead of clearing and redrawing the whole frame, it draws one new wire and
erases only the oldest retained wire with a black line. This economical
rendering method produces the characteristic tiny black gaps where an erased
old wire crosses a newer wire.
.SH OPTIONS
.I mystify
accepts the following options:
.TP 8
.B \-\-window
Draw on a newly-created window. This is the default.
.TP 8
.B \-\-root
Draw on the root window.
.TP 8
.BI \-\-window\-id " number"
Draw on the specified window.
.TP 8
.BI \-\-delay " microseconds"
Delay between animation frames. Default: 30000.
.TP 8
.BI \-\-polys " number"
Number of independently moving polygons. Default: 2.
.TP 8
.BI \-\-points " number"
Number of corners in each polygon. Default: 4.
.TP 8
.BI \-\-trails " number"
Number of old wires retained behind each leading wire. Default: 5.
.TP 8
.BI \-\-speed " number"
Maximum corner velocity in pixels per frame. Default: 14.
.TP 8
.BI \-\-thickness " pixels"
Line thickness. Default: 1.
.TP 8
.BI \-\-colors " number"
Number of hue steps in the color palette. Default: 64.
.TP 8
.BI \-\-seed " number"
Use a deterministic random seed. A value of zero selects a random seed.
.TP 8
.B \-\-fps
Display the current frame rate and CPU load.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP 8
.B DISPLAY
The X display to use.
.TP 8
.B XENVIRONMENT
The resource file that overrides resources stored in the
RESOURCE_MANAGER property.
.TP 8
.B XSCREENSAVER_WINDOW
The window ID supplied by XScreenSaver when running with
.BR \-\-root .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR X (1),
.BR xscreensaver (1)
